      <memberdef kind="function" id="window__geometry_8cc_1a116577f4858558df7da2859fba390465" prot="public" static="no" const="no" explicit="no" inline="no" virt="non-virtual">
        <type>QRect</type>
        <definition>BERNESE_EXPORT QRect bernese::window_utils::NativeWindowGeometry</definition>
        <argsstring>(const QWindow *window)</argsstring>
        <name>NativeWindowGeometry</name>
        <qualifiedname>bernese::window_utils::NativeWindowGeometry</qualifiedname>
        <param>
          <type>const QWindow *</type>
          <declname>window</declname>
        </param>
        <briefdescription>
<para>Read a top-level window&apos;s client rectangle in X11 native pixels. </para>
        </briefdescription>
        <detaileddescription>
<para>Uses public Qt geometry and the window&apos;s own screen and pixel ratio. Call on the GUI thread. This does not create a platform window. Intended for X11 event coordinates and foreign windows; Wayland has no global window origin. Qt exposes integer logical geometry, so reconstructing native pixels can round boundaries that are not representable at the window&apos;s current scale. <parameterlist kind="param"><parameteritem>
<parameternamelist>
<parametername>window</parametername>
</parameternamelist>
<parameterdescription>
<para>Borrowed top-level window, which may be null. </para>
</parameterdescription>
</parameteritem>
</parameterlist>
<simplesect kind="return"><para>Native rectangle, or an empty rectangle if window or screen is null. </para>
</simplesect>
</para>
        </detaileddescription>
        <inbodydescription>
        </inbodydescription>
