        <param>
          <type>const QRect &amp;</type>
          <declname>rect</declname>
        </param>
        <briefdescription>
<para>Moves a top-level widget to a screen and sets its geometry. </para>
        </briefdescription>
        <detaileddescription>
<para>Clamps the size to the widget&apos;s min/max size. Sets the geometry on both the QWidget and its QWindow; the QWindow call fixes stale native sizes after a screen or DPI change.</para>
<para><parameterlist kind="param"><parameteritem>
<parameternamelist>
<parametername>widget</parametername>
</parameternamelist>
<parameterdescription>
<para>Top-level widget. No-op if null or not a window. </para>
</parameterdescription>
</parameteritem>
<parameteritem>
<parameternamelist>
<parametername>screen</parametername>
</parameternamelist>
<parameterdescription>
<para>Target screen, or null to keep the current screen. </para>
</parameterdescription>
</parameteritem>
<parameteritem>
<parameternamelist>
<parametername>rect</parametername>
</parameternamelist>
<parameterdescription>
<para>New geometry in logical pixels. </para>
</parameterdescription>
</parameteritem>
</parameterlist>
</para>
        </detaileddescription>
